+### POST `/api/reharmonize` — Contextual harmonic alternatives
+
+Return three substitution candidates for existing selected chords. The request
+is read-only; only a subsequent editor action applies a candidate. Each patch
+proposes bounded edits within the selection and leaves empty slots untouched.
+
+```json
+{
+  "key": "C major",
+  "timeSignature": [4, 4],
+  "context": [
+    {"measure": 0, "chords": ["Cmaj7", "Am7"]},
+    {"measure": 1, "chords": ["Dm7", "G7"]},
+    {"measure": 2, "chords": ["Cmaj7", null]}
+  ],
+  "selectedSlots": [
+    {"measureIndex": 0, "slotIndex": 0},
+    {"measureIndex": 0, "slotIndex": 1},
+    {"measureIndex": 1, "slotIndex": 0},
+    {"measureIndex": 1, "slotIndex": 1}
+  ],
+  "maxChanges": 4,
+  "mode": "auto",
+  "modelKey": "ft_f1"
+}
+```
+
+Context contains 1–512 consecutive, unique measures with their zero-based score
+numbers (any window of a longer score; it need not start at 0), each with exactly
+two chord slots. `selectedSlots` contains 1–16 unique occupied slots spanning at
+most eight measures, all inside the context. The browser omits empty slots from its selection request.
+`maxChanges` is `1 | 2 | 3 | 4` (default 1), an upper bound per candidate; it does
+not request four alternatives or require exactly four edits. Supported meters
+are 4/4, 3/4, 6/8, 2/4 and 5/4. `mode` defaults to `auto`; explicit `ionian`,
+`dorian`, `phrygian`, `lydian`, `mixolydian`, `aeolian` or `locrian` constrains
+each proposed chord to the corresponding parallel scale.
+
+`ReharmResponse` contains three `candidates`, `modelUsed`, `contextMeasures`,
+`metaModel`, `requestIds`, `costUsd`, `toolCalls`, `modelApproximations`,
+`selection` (`meta`, or `local` when the three were chosen without Meta) and
+`metaUnavailable` (`null`, or why Meta did not choose: `disabled`, `unconfigured`,
+`paused` or `limit`). A local choice has `metaModel: "not used"`.
+Each candidate has an `id`, search `family`, and `changes` containing an address,
+`before`/`after` symbols, shared-tone count, compatible modes and verified
+convention labels. Candidate metrics include pitch distance, bass motion,
+mathematical score, convention score and learned `modelScore`. These metrics
+are not probabilities of musical quality. Model-vocabulary approximations are
+reported separately and never applied as score edits.
+
+The search uses Standard Muse Spark and an available Music Transformer, with
+at most four Meta turns, six tool calls, six scored candidates per family,
+low reasoning effort and 4,096 output tokens per call. The per-call timeout is
+30 seconds and the loop deadline is 100 seconds. The normal request reservation
+cap is $0.15; configured development overrides and public session/day controls
+follow the existing spend policy. Failures are visible: invalid input 422, the
+search's own $0.15 cap 429 (detail without figures), configuration 503, timeout 504,
+other Meta failures 502. No success-shaped fallback substitutes for a failed search.
+When Meta cannot take the request at all, the search runs without it and says so.
+That covers Meta switched off, no key, paused (the credit stop line, the ledger's
+dollar cap with caps on, or a provider with no credit), or the caller's session or
+daily Meta allowance used up (the limiter's 429). It also covers such a stop between
+two Meta turns. Every family is then searched, the Music Transformer scores the
+shortlist, and code offers the best-scoring candidate of each family, with
+`selection: "local"`. Fewer than three distinct candidates is a 422. See
+[search and comparison behavior](docs/reharmonization.md).
+
+### POST `/api/review/candidates` — Second ear
+
+The judge role picks one of a Generate's two or three candidates on facts code computed, and code checks every reason it gives against those facts. Nothing is applied: adopting a candidate stays the user's click.
+
+Request (`ReviewRequest`, strict; HTTP 422 before any fact is computed):
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `key` | The song's key, `C major` or `A minor` |
+| `genre` | One of the 13 genres, or `null` |
+| `sectionType` | The section Generate used, whose song-form rules wrote some slots; `null` = no rules |
+| `original` | The bars before the generation: per measure two slots, a symbol or `null` (1–64 measures) |
+| `candidates` | 2–3 `{label, chords}` over the same measures, every slot as Apply would write it; unique labels |
+| `previousSection` | The section before the bars' section, from the same offset; `null` when there is none |
+
+Facts per candidate, computed by code over its filled slots: `outOfKeyRatio` (chords with a tone outside the key), `changedSlots` (slots that differ from `original`), `repetitionVsPrevious` (chords equal to the previous section's at that slot), `r1Roughness` (mean Sethares roughness per chord, as the R1 rerank computes it; flat roots are respelled for music21) and `rulesSlots` (slots the song-form rules write — context, never a reason).
+
+Response (`ReviewResponse`): `choice`, `reasons: [{fact, factName, value, claim, confirmed, analyzerValue}]` (one or two; `confirmed` when the cited value matches the chosen candidate's fact — counts exactly, ratios and roughness within 0.005 or 1% — otherwise the reason is the model's own statement), `facts`, `provider`, `model`, `requestId`, `costUsd`, `latencyMs`, `source: "judge"`.
+
+Limits: one judge call (`LLM_JUDGE_*`, Muse Spark by default), effort `low`, 30 s, 2048 output tokens including reasoning, $0.03 reserved (an open-weight judge's one JSON-guard retry counts twice). Statuses: 503 `THEARTIST_META_ENABLED=0` ("disabled") or missing configuration; 429 budget or a spend limit; 504 timeout; 502 invalid reply. A failure answers `{detail, error: {kind, message, requestId}, provider, model, costUsd, latencyMs}` and never a fallback order.
